WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.787
This episode focuses on geographic fit.

2
00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:11.807
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:16.775
Census geography is a system of legal, administrative, and statistical areas.

4
00:00:16.775 --> 00:00:25.099
A place, county subdivision, tract, block group, public use microdata area, and ZIP Code Tabulation Area are not interchangeable.

5
00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:28.809
Choose geography based on the decision and product availability.

6
00:00:28.809 --> 00:00:33.853
Tracts and block groups support small-area analysis, but estimates can be less precise.

7
00:00:33.853 --> 00:00:39.592
Boundaries can change, and a service district or neighborhood may not match a standard Census area.

8
00:00:39.592 --> 00:00:41.992
Save geographic codes, not only names.

9
00:00:41.992 --> 00:00:47.107
Use official relationship files or a documented crosswalk when boundaries differ.

10
00:00:47.107 --> 00:00:54.495
If an analyst aggregates areas, record the method and avoid claiming exact alignment where only approximation exists.

11
00:00:54.495 --> 00:00:55.939
Torrance application segment.

12
00:00:55.939 --> 00:00:59.476
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

13
00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:10.732
The cited City of Torrance primary source is General Plan, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/Departments-Offices/Departments-Offices/Community-Development/Planning-Division/Comprehensive-Planning/General-Plan.

14
00:01:10.732 --> 00:01:17.107
For a local analysis, identify the policy geography in the General Plan before choosing Census areas, and disclose any mismatch.

15
00:01:17.107 --> 00:01:24.130
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

16
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:34.453
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

17
00:01:34.453 --> 00:01:37.810
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

18
00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.750
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

19
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.183
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

20
00:01:47.183 --> 00:01:53.389
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

21
00:01:53.389 --> 00:01:57.886
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
